WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:02.950 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  roshan the camel is a bit of a celebrity  here  whenever he clops through children know  he's bringing some exciting tales to  their village  books to help them with their reading at  first i tried to read the books myself  but if i do not understand anything i  ask the teacher  i prefer picture books because when i  look at the pictures and the photographs  i can understand the story better  the camel library began moving in august  roshan takes books to four villages in  the manned region  of pakistan's southern baluchistan  province which has the lowest literacy  rate in the country  at just 40 percent rahima jalal started  the project with the help of ngos  in addition to keeping children busy  she's also helping their parents  when the coronavirus spread the entire  region all the schools were closed there  was an atmosphere of depression  for old and young alike there's no  entertainment for the children at all in  the region where i live  the only activity for the children is to  go to school and then go back home  murad ali owns the camel and used it to  carry firewood through remote and rugged  areas to market that was before he was  approached with a better offer  i was asked if i would like to carry  books on my camel i was surprised  and thought how can i carry books on my  camel but now i carry them to four  villages and the children love it  i'm also very happy so are people in the  villages so it's an ongoing thing  and i'm happy to do it  most of the budget around 120 dollars a  month goes to employ the camel  those behind the project plan to expand  to more villages once they find support  but for now the kids have picked the  books of their choice and say goodbye  until next time  andrew chappelle al jazeera

